      "writtenOn": "2025-08-30T17:01:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I guess we put `start()` in a separate thread so that the `time.sleep(delay)` doesn\u0027t affect the completion of this method. But this should be safe because `v2_playbook_on_task_start()` isn\u0027t going to hang around for long after that sleep completes. Mostly thinking out loud here to ensure we aren\u0027t introducing a memory leak by having a bunch of threads with references to self (and self._log, etc).",
